    * Uses only the arrival times supplied via `inputs`.
    * Uses the motion‑log positions to detect collisions.
    * A collision is declared when two arrived objects appear within a distance
      less than or equal to the largest recorded collision distance for this
      scope (max of the distances seen in the actual dataset).  This
      ensures that all recorded collisions are reproduced while avoiding
      earlier spurious matches.
    * Only outcomes that occur at or after `start` are returned.
    """
